PART III — INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY PROTECTION

11. SOURCE CODE RIGHTS

11.1 Original source code lawfully owned by Rail Design AI is protected under applicable intellectual property laws.

11.2 Source-code access does not grant unrestricted redistribution or resale rights.

11.3 Developers must respect confidentiality and access restrictions established by their agreements.

11.4 Source-code ownership must be determined according to actual authorship, employment arrangements, assignments, and applicable law.

12. APPLICATION ARCHITECTURE

Original architecture, implementation details, and proprietary technical designs may be protected to the extent recognized by applicable law.

Unauthorized copying of protected original implementation materials is prohibited.

13. USER INTERFACE AND DESIGNS

Original interface layouts, graphics, illustrations, and visual materials may be protected under applicable copyright and design laws.

This provision does not claim exclusive ownership of general design concepts, standard interface patterns, or independently created designs.

14. TRADEMARKS AND BRANDING

The name Rail Design AI and its associated logos or brand assets may be subject to trademark protection.

No licensee automatically receives permission to register or use confusingly similar branding.

Use of company branding must be authorized where required.

This Agreement does not establish that a trademark registration has already been obtained.

15. DOCUMENTATION

Original technical documentation and written materials may be protected by copyright.

Users may access documentation for authorized software operation.

Commercial reproduction or redistribution requires permission where applicable.

