16.1 The software may incorporate open-source libraries, frameworks, tools, or dependencies.

16.2 Such components remain subject to their original licenses.

16.3 This Agreement does not replace or override third-party license terms.

16.4 Any applicable attribution, notice, source-disclosure, or redistribution obligations must be respected.

16.5 Where a third-party license grants rights that conflict with a restriction in this Agreement, the applicable third-party license governs that component.

17. EXTERNAL SERVICES AND APIs

The software may connect to external providers, APIs, hosting platforms, authentication services, payment processors, or cloud infrastructure.

Such services remain subject to their respective terms and conditions.

Rail Design AI does not claim ownership of external provider services.

18. THIRD-PARTY BRANDING

Third-party company names, logos, trademarks, and product identities remain the property of their respective owners.

Their appearance in the software does not imply ownership or endorsement.

