PART VIII — TERMINATION AND ENFORCEMENT

33. TERMINATION

A license may expire or be terminated according to its applicable terms.

Serious violations may result in suspension or termination of authorization, subject to applicable law and contractual requirements.

34. EFFECT OF TERMINATION

Following lawful termination, the licensee must discontinue use to the extent required by the applicable agreement.

Any obligations that legally survive termination will remain effective.

35. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY ENFORCEMENT

Unauthorized exploitation of protected intellectual property may result in legal remedies where supported by applicable law.

Any enforcement action must respect applicable procedural and substantive legal requirements.

36. INDEMNIFICATION

Any indemnification obligations must be established in an applicable written agreement and interpreted subject to applicable law.

No unlimited indemnification obligation is created merely by this section.

