PART IX — LEGAL AND ADMINISTRATIVE TERMS

37. GOVERNING LAW

The governing law and jurisdiction must be identified in a finalized version of this Agreement.

Mandatory legal protections remain applicable regardless of contractual wording.

38. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

The parties should attempt to resolve disputes through good-faith communication where appropriate.

Mediation, arbitration, or court proceedings may be used according to the applicable agreement and law.

39. SEVERABILITY

If any provision is found invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply to the extent legally permitted.

40. NO WAIVER

Failure to enforce a provision does not automatically constitute a permanent waiver of that provision.

41. ASSIGNMENT

A licensee may not transfer or sublicense its license without the required authorization, except where applicable law provides otherwise.

42. ENTIRE AGREEMENT

This Agreement governs the licensing matters addressed herein, subject to applicable written agreements, third-party licenses, privacy policies, and mandatory law.

43. AMENDMENTS

Any revision must be made through an appropriately authorized written update.

The version number and effective date should be updated when material changes are made.

44. ELECTRONIC ACCEPTANCE

Where legally valid, acceptance may be recorded electronically through an appropriate agreement process.

The applicable consent and notice requirements must be followed.

45. LANGUAGE AND INTERPRETATION

This Agreement is written in English.

If translated, the applicable governing agreement should specify which version controls in the event of a discrepancy, subject to mandatory law.

